17:def main(input_grid):
18:    """
19:    Expand a vertical colored line into a centered alternating-color pyramid.
20:
21:    Input structure:
22:    - The input contains one non-black line segment on a black background.
23:    - The line's dominant column gives the pyramid center column.
24:    - The line length determines the pyramid height and widest row.
25:
26:    Rule:
27:    - Identify the line color, center column, and lowest occupied row.
28:    - Build a black output grid of the same size.
29:    - For each row above the line base, draw a centered run whose colors alternate by distance from the center.
30:
31:    Key insight:
32:    - The original line is the pyramid axis; moving upward shortens the run, while
33:      horizontal parity controls the alternating colors.
34:    """
35:    # Plan (from the original seed solver):
36:    # 1. Parse the input
37:    # 2. Draw the left side of the pyramid
